    <!-- ===================================================
             PHASE 3 ADVANTAGES
             =================================================== -->
    <hr class="p3-sep" />

    <div class="p3-section-label">Design Advantages</div>
    <h2 class="p3-section-title">Phase 3 vs. Phase 2 improvements</h2>

    <div class="p3-phase-grid">
        <div class="p3-phase-card" data-num="1">
            <h3>Simplified Power Bus</h3>
            <p>Single unified battery eliminates dual-bus routing and cross-charging logic. Reduced wiring complexity and potential failure points.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-phase-card" data-num="2">
            <h3>Open-Rail Architecture</h3>
            <p>Pistons operate along exposed rails (locomotive-style), preventing oil and water accumulation in sealed chamber walls.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-phase-card" data-num="3">
            <h3>Direct Wheel Coupling</h3>
            <p>Connecting rods attach piston travel directly to wheel hubs. No crankshaft wear, fewer rotating seals, cleaner mechanical interface.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-phase-card" data-num="4">
            <h3>Atmospheric Pressure Zones</h3>
            <p>Linear pistons in open rails mean no trapped pressure pockets. Steam escapes safely; no condensation pools or corrosion zones.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ===================================================
             PHASE 3 FLAWS / DESIGN CONSIDERATIONS
             ===================================================== -->
    <div class="p3-section-label">Design Considerations</div>
    <h2 class="p3-section-title">Phase 3 trade-offs and constraints</h2>

    <div class="p3-flaw-grid">
        <div class="p3-flaw major">
            <div class="p3-flaw-tag">Major Consideration</div>
            <h4>Rail Friction & Wear</h4>
            <p>Open rails require continuous lubrication and bearing maintenance. Dust and debris can accumulate on slide surfaces.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-flaw thermal">
            <div class="p3-flaw-tag">Thermal Challenge</div>
            <h4>Steam Escape Losses</h4>
            <p>Atmospheric exposure increases thermal losses compared to sealed piston chambers. Insulation and recovery systems needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-flaw design">
            <div class="p3-flaw-tag">Design Constraint</div>
            <h4>Linkage Geometry</h4>
            <p>Converting linear rail motion to wheel rotation requires precise connecting rod angles. Mechanical losses in conversion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p3-flaw critical">
            <div class="p3-flaw-tag">Critical Requirement</div>
            <h4>Pressure Vessel Safety</h4>
            <p>Single reservoir must maintain rigorous pressure relief and monitoring. No redundant battery backup path if system fails.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>


